. Clock & Counter
Use a 10 ns clock period (100 MHz clock).

A modulo-10 counter increments every 10 ns.

Each counter value corresponds to one phase of operation.

2. Phase Mapping
Counter Value	Time (ns)	Signal Activated	Behavior
0	0–10	rs, rt	Register addresses decoded
1	10–20	read_data1, read_data2	Values read from Register File
2	20–30	alu_out	ALU performs operation
3	30–40	write_data	Result written back
4–9	40–100	Continuous ALU results	ALU updates each cycle


3. Control Logic
Decoder: Converts counter output into control signals.

Enable signals: Each stage (Register File, ALU, Write-back) is enabled only during its assigned interval.

Continuous mode: After cycle 4, ALU keeps updating results until counter resets.

4. Implementation Options
Synchronous FSM: States S0–S4 mapped to operations, looping every 100 ns.

Ring Counter: Easier hardware implementation, each stage gets a dedicated pulse.

Verilog Example:

verilog
always @(posedge clk) begin
  case(counter)
    0: begin enable_decode <= 1; end
    1: begin enable_read <= 1; end
    2: begin enable_alu <= 1; end
    3: begin enable_write <= 1; end
    default: begin enable_alu <= 1; end // continuous update
  endcase
end
